# NOTE=PRE-HANDLER MASKED WAIT DIAGNOSTIC, PHYSICALLY EXECUTED 2026-09-18, one run, no Game Pak. It is NOT a GBP-VIDEO-002 run that reached its scientific target and must never be counted as one: it ended on stop=safety_budget, status=ok_no_change_inconclusive, capture_s=174.892, valid_s=119.608 against a 120 s target, valid_at_target=0 - the 5 s pause sits inside the 180 s safety budget, so the budget expired 0.392 s short. The question it was built to answer is answered by its first six seconds.
# NOTE=THE RESULT: after stage A put CONTROL in the running shape, the probe waited with PI masked, no handler installed and no service in flight. Requested 5000 ms, want_ticks 202500000, elapsed 202500009 ticks at 40.5 MHz = 5.00000022 s, 78307256 iterations, done=1 (the time bound, not the iteration cap). Read-only snapshots either side: CONTROL 8c -> 8c, IRQ semantic 0500 -> 0500, INTSR 00012000 -> 00012000, INTMR 000001fa -> 000001fa. Nothing observable moved. GBP-HW-116.
# NOTE=SERVICE RESUMED NORMALLY. Handler install rc=ok old_handler=null, PREUNMASK ok=1 control=8c irq=0500/0500, first delivery at 89 ticks (~2 us) of handler latency. 1108063 unmasks = deliveries = acks = rearms; timeouts 0, busy 0, uncertain 0, overflow 0; 10446 frames (10445 complete, 1 incomplete, 2 resync), baseline valid at frame 4. Clean teardown: CONTROL restored to 90 with readback, IRQ stop written and read back, PI cleanup with no sticky bit, AR_INFO 0043 restored with readback, handler restored, mask_ok=1, intmr_final=000001fa. GBP-HW-117, GBP-HW-118.
# NOTE=THE CLAIM IS THE DURATION AND THE POSITION EXERCISED, AND NOTHING MORE. 5 s at that point, on this unit, under these conditions. Nothing here licenses 10 s, 30 s or an unbounded wait, and nothing here says what the AGB was displaying: the probe reads no VIDEO before the handler exists.
# NOTE=THIRTY-EIGHT SEMANTIC DISAGREEMENTS, the R3 shape again: 38 SOURCE_SERVICED, 0 SOURCE_OTHER, 0 NON_SOURCE, 38 disc-extra, 0 majority-extra, 0 quarantined, 0 deferred, follow-up present 38/38. A third corroboration of the policy under an unusual startup, not new information about the mechanism: U-GBP-033 stays OPEN. GBP-HW-119.
# NOTE=IDENTITY WARNING. What was physically validated is the vstate-prewait-5000 VARIANT at commit 500429a with DOL sha256 b5f0060a... A rebuild at any other commit produces a DIFFERENT hash, because the commit identity is embedded in the image, and inherits the source behaviour but NOT the physical status. Compare hashes before calling any rebuilt DOL the tested artifact.
# NOTE=THIS SCRIPT IS A PREFIX, NOT THE RUN, exactly as in the other vstate fixtures: it carries the 003A stage, the pre-handler wait with its WAITPRE/WAITPOST snapshots, the verify cycles and the teardown - the only parts whose transport operations the log records. The remaining lean cycles were never written and are NOT invented here. The sidecar is the evidence for them: 10446 frame records, 11 events, 38 diagnostics, 2 AUDIO blocks. Header CRC 7fe06338, total CRC 4315e14a, both recomputed on analysis.
# NOTE=THE SOURCE LOG DECLARES truncated=1. The truncated line is PREHANDLERWAIT, which hit the logger's 255-character limit and ends at "intmr_po". It costs nothing: the WAITPRE and WAITPOST snapshots record CONTROL, IRQ, INTSR and INTMR separately and in full, and that is where every value above comes from. Registered as an INSTRUMENTATION DEFECT / NON-BLOCKING.
